WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.919
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.189 --> 00:03.442
[♪ theme song playing]

3
00:03.525 --> 00:04.651
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

4
00:04.735 --> 00:06.028
START DATING...

5
00:36.725 --> 00:41.063
BETWEEN STEPS

6
00:41.688 --> 00:43.940
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:44.024 --> 00:45.651
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

8
01:02.000 --> 01:03.126
It's salty.

9
01:03.210 --> 01:04.211
Salty?

10
01:04.294 --> 01:05.295
Yes.

11
01:07.005 --> 01:11.343
To me, it tasted kind of sweet... It was sweet.

12
01:14.680 --> 01:17.683
[♪ theme song playing]

13
01:21.478 --> 01:23.146
[both grunting]

14
01:24.731 --> 01:26.316
Wait. Wait a second.

15
01:26.400 --> 01:28.568
Calm down and get a hold of yourself.

16
01:29.361 --> 01:30.696
Youjin.

17
01:32.322 --> 01:33.740
Wait.

18
01:33.824 --> 01:35.200
Wait...

19
01:51.133 --> 01:52.134
[Lim Youjin grunting]

20
01:52.217 --> 01:53.218
-My stomach. -Oh?

21
01:53.301 --> 01:54.803
-Why? What's wrong? -[Lim Youjin yelps]

22
01:54.886 --> 01:55.887
My stomach hurts.

23
01:55.971 --> 01:57.180
-Hey. -It hurts so much.

24
01:57.264 --> 01:59.558
Why? Something happened to your stomach?

25
01:59.641 --> 02:01.643
-Let me see. -[muttering in pain]

26
02:34.885 --> 02:37.888
[water running]

27
03:11.463 --> 03:13.465
[song fades]

28
03:14.007 --> 03:15.133
EPISODE 5

29
03:15.217 --> 03:16.468
-[Park Minjae] Are you okay? -[sighs]

30
03:17.260 --> 03:19.262
-What are you doing? -It's porridge.

31
03:19.805 --> 03:21.473
You have to eat something, right?

32
03:22.015 --> 03:23.391
You know how to make porridge?

33
03:23.475 --> 03:25.560
I'm just boiling some rice with water.

34
03:25.936 --> 03:26.937
Mm-hmm.

35
03:29.356 --> 03:30.690
You farted, right?

36
03:31.274 --> 03:32.275
What?

37
03:33.610 --> 03:35.695
Why would I fart? I don't fart.

38
03:35.779 --> 03:38.990
You're supposed to fart before eating. You know, for digestion...

39
03:39.991 --> 03:41.743
-Because of the surgery? -Yeah.

40
03:43.203 --> 03:44.329
Well...

41
03:47.290 --> 03:49.793
Wait, do you hear that?

42
03:50.877 --> 03:52.379
-Hear what? -[phone vibrating]

43
03:52.462 --> 03:54.297
Oh. No, it's not me.

44
03:56.758 --> 03:58.635
No, I think your phone's ringing.

45
03:58.718 --> 03:59.803
Hmm?

46
04:00.804 --> 04:02.931
[Lim Youseong] Hey, why weren't you answering your phone?

47
04:03.014 --> 04:04.182
Your mom's worried sick.

48
04:04.266 --> 04:05.350
Did she pick up?

49
04:05.433 --> 04:06.643
Yeah, she picked up.

50
04:06.726 --> 04:07.727
Goodness.

51
04:08.311 --> 04:10.063
Go out? Where would I go?

52
04:10.146 --> 04:12.315
I just had surgery, and my stomach is killing me.

53
04:14.609 --> 04:16.653
No, I'm home.

54
04:17.279 --> 04:19.698
But I was in the bathroom, so I didn't hear my phone.

55
04:19.781 --> 04:20.907
Why?

56
04:20.991 --> 04:22.576
What do you mean? You little brat!

57
04:22.659 --> 04:23.660
Jeez!

58
04:24.160 --> 04:25.328
Oh, no! [grunts]

59
04:27.122 --> 04:28.206
Hey, it's Mom.

60
04:28.790 --> 04:29.791
Did you have lunch?

61
04:31.042 --> 04:33.879
I made some porridge and put it in the fridge.

62
04:34.796 --> 04:36.631
Heat it up, eat first, then take your meds.

63
04:36.715 --> 04:38.842
And don't read. Just get some sleep.

64
04:38.925 --> 04:40.302
Okay, will do.

65
04:40.385 --> 04:43.597
I'll eat the porridge, take my medicine, and go to bed. No reading.

66
04:45.682 --> 04:47.142
No, I won't study.

67
04:47.225 --> 04:48.310
Okay. Bye.

68
04:48.393 --> 04:50.020
-Bye. -Wait.

69
04:50.103 --> 04:51.104
Hey, Lim Youjin.

70
04:51.187 --> 04:52.397
Be honest with me.

71
04:52.480 --> 04:54.274
-You're not home now, are you? -[Seo Miyoung] Come on.

72
04:54.357 --> 04:56.735
What are you talking about? I'm home.

73
04:56.818 --> 04:57.819
Yeah?

74
04:58.361 --> 04:59.946
Then turn on the TV.

75
05:00.030 --> 05:01.031
No.

76
05:02.324 --> 05:03.325
[line disconnects]

77
05:03.408 --> 05:05.285
[Park Minjae] Why? What's up?

78
05:05.368 --> 05:07.621
I'm sorry. I'll have porridge another time.

79
05:07.704 --> 05:09.289
I need to get home right now.

80
05:09.372 --> 05:10.457
What?

81
05:11.166 --> 05:12.250
What's going on?

82
05:12.876 --> 05:14.544
Well... I'm sorry.

83
05:14.628 --> 05:16.004
[♪ theme song playing]

84
05:16.087 --> 05:18.632
No, wait a second. Hey.

85
05:20.759 --> 05:22.510
[Lim Yongseok] What did you order?

86
05:22.594 --> 05:25.096
-Did you order mackerel? -Yeah, and one kimchi jjim too.

87
05:26.056 --> 05:27.140
Hey, what's going on?

88
05:28.558 --> 05:30.268
-Dad, give me the car key. -Huh?

89
05:30.352 --> 05:31.603
The car key.

90
05:32.979 --> 05:33.980
The car key.

91
05:41.363 --> 05:43.990
I don't mind taking you home. Really.

92
05:44.658 --> 05:46.576
It's okay. I can go by myself.

93
05:47.077 --> 05:50.163
But you're sick. How can you go by yourself? Are you sure?

94
05:50.246 --> 05:51.873
Of course. I'm going to take a taxi.

95
05:53.166 --> 05:54.626
[groaning]

96
05:54.709 --> 05:56.127
Which way is it coming from?

97
06:04.469 --> 06:05.470
I'll call you.

98
06:06.137 --> 06:07.931
-Are you sure you'll be fine? -Yeah.

99
06:10.225 --> 06:11.643
Okay. Bye then.

100
06:24.990 --> 06:26.574
Sir. Could you go a little faster?

101
06:26.658 --> 06:27.742
-I need to hurry. -[driver] Okay.

102
07:07.657 --> 07:09.325
Excuse me, sir. Your car...

103
07:10.201 --> 07:11.369
[car alarm beeps]

104
07:47.280 --> 07:49.282
[music ends]

105
07:49.365 --> 07:50.366
[sighs]

106
07:53.995 --> 07:56.206
How long do I have to keep eating porridge?

107
07:57.123 --> 07:58.333
Just a few more days.

108
07:58.416 --> 08:00.168
It's easier to digest than rice.

109
08:01.294 --> 08:02.712
Once you get your stitches out,

110
08:02.796 --> 08:04.714
ask the doctor if you can eat regular food.

111
08:04.798 --> 08:05.799
Okay.

112
08:10.553 --> 08:11.679
[Seo Miyoung sighs]

113
08:11.763 --> 08:13.223
What is it now?

114
08:13.306 --> 08:15.642
Are you on a hunger strike? Aren't you going to eat?

115
08:16.392 --> 08:18.728
Hey, then what was with those rings?

116
08:20.021 --> 08:21.439
I saw them, you little brat.

117
08:21.523 --> 08:23.858
I saw them hidden in your drawer.

118
08:24.859 --> 08:27.070
Hey, did you go through my room again?

119
08:27.153 --> 08:29.322
Don't you "hey" me. I'm your big brother!

120
08:29.405 --> 08:32.033
That's right, I went through your room. So what?

121
08:32.116 --> 08:34.786
[groans] Mom, Lim Youseong went through my room again.

122
08:34.869 --> 08:37.705
Well, I tried to stop him, but...

123
08:38.623 --> 08:41.417
You dummy, why couldn't you just keep quiet?

124
08:41.501 --> 08:44.712
Fine. It wasn't nice of me to go through your room. I accept that.

125
08:44.796 --> 08:46.297
But what was with those rings?

126
08:46.381 --> 08:47.757
Aren't they matching rings?

127
08:49.342 --> 08:51.386
I saw them, okay?

128
08:51.469 --> 08:53.680
Are you seriously going to keep playing dumb?

129
08:54.889 --> 08:57.350
You've been lying and seeing some guy behind our backs.

130
08:57.433 --> 08:58.643
You little sneak.

131
08:59.227 --> 09:00.228
Come on.

132
09:00.311 --> 09:03.189
What do you mean, Youjin is seeing a guy behind our backs?

133
09:03.273 --> 09:05.483
You're just busy studying, right?

134
09:06.109 --> 09:08.236
Hey, knock it off and eat your food.

135
09:08.319 --> 09:11.030
Wow. I mean, I'm not the only one who saw the rings here.

136
09:11.739 --> 09:13.491
Hey. Hey, you.

137
09:13.575 --> 09:15.660
Mom and Dad saw them too. Okay?

138
09:15.743 --> 09:18.496
I showed them a picture of the rings, you little brat.

139
09:22.834 --> 09:26.588
Well, we just... I didn't mean to see it.

140
09:26.671 --> 09:28.381
He just shoved it in our faces.

141
09:29.090 --> 09:32.010
But we wanted to respect your privacy,

142
09:32.093 --> 09:34.637
so we didn't bring it up, even though we were curious.

143
09:34.721 --> 09:36.556
See? Mom is curious too.

144
09:37.557 --> 09:39.517
Did those rings

145
09:40.101 --> 09:43.438
have my name or initials engraved on them?

146
09:46.316 --> 09:48.943
So... they're not your rings?

147
09:49.736 --> 09:50.737
They're not yours?

148
09:52.906 --> 09:53.907
Now,

149
09:54.908 --> 09:56.951
let me present a hypothesis

150
09:57.035 --> 09:59.245
that's mathematical, logical, and philosophical.

151
09:59.329 --> 10:00.914
It's only a hypothesis, though.

152
10:01.331 --> 10:02.332
[Lim Youseong sighs]

153
10:02.415 --> 10:05.793
Detective Conan, one truth prevails!

154
10:07.879 --> 10:11.966
What if they were Lim Youseong's rings to begin with, not mine?

155
10:12.592 --> 10:13.593
What?

156
10:15.053 --> 10:18.223
He'd actually had those rings for a long time.

157
10:18.723 --> 10:21.059
He had bought them for his girlfriend at the time,

158
10:21.142 --> 10:23.102
but she turned down his proposal.

159
10:24.187 --> 10:27.190
Then he used those same rings to frame his younger sister.

160
10:27.941 --> 10:29.192
Are you nuts?

161
10:29.275 --> 10:32.779
Come on. Would he really go that far just to frame you? Why?

162
10:33.363 --> 10:36.366
I know you guys fight all the time, but that's too much...

163
10:37.367 --> 10:41.287
Because his younger sister knows one of his secrets.

164
10:41.871 --> 10:43.873
Secret? What is it?

165
10:45.959 --> 10:49.128
The truth is, those rings actually belonged...

166
10:51.297 --> 10:55.134
to a former employee of Cheil Auto Repair Shop, Lee Jihye--

167
10:55.218 --> 10:56.970
-Hey! You little... -Jeez, you scared me.

168
11:00.348 --> 11:01.724
[exhales sharply]

169
11:03.393 --> 11:04.394
You're real nasty.

170
11:07.188 --> 11:08.189
What...

171
11:12.777 --> 11:13.778
Lee Jihye?

172
11:14.737 --> 11:17.407
From last year... No, was it two years ago?

173
11:18.116 --> 11:20.576
That girl who used to work at our office, right?

174
11:20.660 --> 11:23.746
Yeah. So that's why she quit.

175
11:24.163 --> 11:25.164
Oh.

176
11:25.248 --> 11:26.749
How did you know about that?

177
11:27.333 --> 11:29.544
I don't. That was just a hypothesis.

178
11:31.629 --> 11:33.798
Jeez, that was mean.

179
11:34.299 --> 11:38.136
You go to Seohan National University. Don't stoop to his level.

180
11:39.095 --> 11:40.096
Yeah.

181
11:41.222 --> 11:43.641
Have some compassion for him.

182
11:43.725 --> 11:46.436
[breath trembling]

183
11:46.519 --> 11:49.147
[quietly] I will find you at all costs.

184
11:50.064 --> 11:54.110
I will find you and make you pay, you little...

185
11:57.238 --> 12:00.241
[breath trembling]

186
12:09.250 --> 12:11.252
[massager vibrating]

187
12:11.419 --> 12:14.422
[♪ pensive music playing]

188
12:16.716 --> 12:18.301
[sighs]

189
12:21.846 --> 12:22.847
[massager stops]

190
12:29.187 --> 12:30.188
[grunts]

191
12:52.919 --> 12:55.922
[Kim Sejin muttering] X and Y already knew each other.

192
12:56.422 --> 13:00.093
X was in fashion and textiles, and Y is in mechanical engineering.

193
13:02.678 --> 13:05.181
How did they know each other from different departments?

194
13:06.015 --> 13:07.225
X...

195
13:07.892 --> 13:11.813
had also gone on blind dates with C, D, and E,

196
13:12.939 --> 13:14.148
all arranged by Y.

197
13:14.232 --> 13:15.233
Why?

198
13:16.401 --> 13:18.528
[sighing heavily]

199
13:19.487 --> 13:22.782
[inhales] X had tried to meet Y in private.

200
13:22.865 --> 13:24.283
Even went to Y's house.

201
13:24.826 --> 13:25.827
Why?

202
13:29.330 --> 13:30.706
Is X a man-eater?

203
13:31.749 --> 13:32.917
A queen bee?

204
13:33.000 --> 13:34.001
Beekeeping?

205
13:34.752 --> 13:36.504
Y is kind of clueless.

206
13:38.089 --> 13:41.592
Into married women?

207
13:43.970 --> 13:46.722
But what would those two have to talk about in private?

208
13:48.975 --> 13:50.184
Some kind of secret?

209
13:52.562 --> 13:55.857
References. I need references.

210
14:12.456 --> 14:13.457
[sighs]

211
14:24.051 --> 14:25.052
[indistinct chatter]

212
14:30.433 --> 14:32.185
-[sighs] -[soft tinkling]

213
14:42.737 --> 14:43.905
[door opens]

214
14:44.697 --> 14:46.324
Hey, good morning.

215
14:46.908 --> 14:48.075
[Kim Sejin] Hello.

216
14:53.039 --> 14:55.458
So Lim Youjin is coming back to the lab starting today?

217
14:55.541 --> 14:56.542
Huh?

218
14:57.251 --> 14:58.544
Yeah, she is.

219
14:59.587 --> 15:01.005
[Kim Sejin] But she hasn't shown up yet.

220
15:05.760 --> 15:07.470
It's not time yet.

221
15:07.553 --> 15:08.554
Nobody's here.

222
15:20.274 --> 15:22.902
So, what was...

223
15:24.862 --> 15:27.198
Lim Youjin doing at your place that day?

224
15:29.367 --> 15:30.743
That day?

225
15:30.826 --> 15:33.162
She had a question about something in a paper.

226
15:33.746 --> 15:37.500
Well, then she could've just emailed or called you.

227
15:38.918 --> 15:41.337
I know. So I told her to just email me next time.

228
15:43.256 --> 15:44.257
[sighing]

229
15:46.634 --> 15:47.677
What?

230
15:49.971 --> 15:51.138
-Nothing. -[door opens]

231
15:51.222 --> 15:52.556
Hello.

232
15:52.640 --> 15:54.058
-[Kim Sejin] Hello. -Hi.

233
15:56.686 --> 15:58.312
Good morning.

234
15:58.396 --> 15:59.522
Hello.

235
15:59.605 --> 16:00.773
[door closes]

236
16:16.497 --> 16:17.581
[honking]

237
16:31.846 --> 16:34.473
Call me when you're done. I'll come pick you up.

238
16:36.434 --> 16:37.852
I can get home by myself.

239
16:38.644 --> 16:41.605
You don't have to drive me anymore. My stitches are out. I'm fine.

240
16:41.689 --> 16:43.316
Mom is worried.

241
16:44.317 --> 16:45.818
Let me drive you a few more days.

242
16:49.613 --> 16:50.614
[both sighing]

243
16:50.698 --> 16:52.700
Look, you started it, okay?

244
16:53.534 --> 16:55.745
Why did you have to go through my room?

245
16:56.370 --> 16:58.164
Dude, you crossed the line first.

246
16:58.247 --> 17:00.249
"Dude"? Did you just call me "dude"?

247
17:01.208 --> 17:03.085
Hey, you know what?

248
17:03.169 --> 17:05.504
You've always disrespected me like that.

249
17:06.005 --> 17:09.633
And I've always let it slide because you're my only sister.

250
17:09.717 --> 17:11.218
I told myself, "Fine, it's cute."

251
17:11.302 --> 17:13.929
"Go ahead and walk all over me. Do whatever you want."

252
17:14.013 --> 17:15.681
But this time, you crossed the line.

253
17:16.724 --> 17:17.725
Sorry.

254
17:17.808 --> 17:20.436
Save it. Don't bother apologizing. I won't accept it.

255
17:20.519 --> 17:21.854
From now on, we're at war.

256
17:23.189 --> 17:25.775
I'll find your boyfriend no matter what it takes,

257
17:25.858 --> 17:28.569
and I'm going to expose you for the snake you really are.

258
17:28.652 --> 17:29.654
Now get lost.

259
17:29.737 --> 17:31.906
-Get out! Go. -[scoffs]

260
17:38.663 --> 17:39.664
Youjin.

261
17:41.207 --> 17:42.625
One truth prevails.

262
17:43.542 --> 17:44.543
Freak.

263
17:44.627 --> 17:46.629
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

264
18:04.146 --> 18:05.356
[tires screeching]

265
18:08.818 --> 18:10.820
[♪ music increases in tempo]

266
18:21.831 --> 18:22.832
Youseong.

267
18:23.833 --> 18:25.000
Subin. Hey.

268
18:26.335 --> 18:27.461
What are you doing here?

269
18:29.130 --> 18:30.965
-How about we sit here? -Yeah, sure.

270
18:37.513 --> 18:40.391
How come you don't come over anymore? Are you that busy?

271
18:40.516 --> 18:43.519
Uh, yeah, pretty busy.

272
18:43.602 --> 18:46.605
I need to study and have lab work to do.

273
18:46.689 --> 18:47.815
That's why.

274
18:47.898 --> 18:50.234
But what brings you to our campus?

275
18:50.317 --> 18:54.363
Youjin had her appendix taken out, so I'm giving her rides for a few days.

276
18:54.947 --> 18:57.199
Right, I heard about her surgery. I meant to visit.

277
18:57.283 --> 18:58.659
She's already back at the lab?

278
18:58.743 --> 19:01.412
Getting your appendix out is hardly even surgery, you know.

279
19:01.495 --> 19:03.789
She got out quickly, and she's been eating fine.

280
19:03.873 --> 19:05.791
Really? That's great to hear.

281
19:06.792 --> 19:09.170
A little later, and it would have been bad.

282
19:09.253 --> 19:12.339
But someone got her to the hospital before her appendix burst,

283
19:12.965 --> 19:16.427
so they got to operate on time, and she's recovering pretty fast.

284
19:16.510 --> 19:17.720
That's a relief.

285
19:18.721 --> 19:23.726
And I heard the person who took her to the hospital was a professor here.

286
19:23.809 --> 19:24.935
Do you know who it is?

287
19:25.019 --> 19:26.020
What?

288
19:26.520 --> 19:27.646
A professor?

289
19:27.730 --> 19:30.065
I hear he's tall and handsome.

290
19:30.566 --> 19:33.402
He's a professor in his early to mid-30s.

291
19:34.069 --> 19:36.280
I mean, are there professors that young?

292
19:37.156 --> 19:38.282
I'm not sure.

293
19:39.158 --> 19:40.618
Isn't he one of your professors?

294
19:41.202 --> 19:43.913
No, we don't have any professors like that in our department.

295
19:43.996 --> 19:45.039
Oh!

296
19:45.122 --> 19:47.124
Maybe he's a mechanical engineering professor?

297
19:47.208 --> 19:49.293
There's a professor like that there?

298
19:50.336 --> 19:53.964
I actually don't know much about that department.

299
19:54.048 --> 19:55.341
You should ask Youjin.

300
19:55.424 --> 19:57.259
She won't tell me, so...

301
19:57.885 --> 19:58.886
Why not?

302
19:59.845 --> 20:00.846
Hmm...

303
20:01.806 --> 20:04.099
Oh! Could it be him?

304
20:04.183 --> 20:05.351
Who?

305
20:05.434 --> 20:08.187
There's this tall and handsome...

306
20:08.854 --> 20:11.357
But he's not a professor. He's just an assistant.

307
20:11.941 --> 20:14.652
He's an assistant, not a professor?

308
20:14.735 --> 20:16.028
Ah.

309
20:16.987 --> 20:18.489
What's his name?

310
20:19.073 --> 20:20.074
Oh.

311
20:21.283 --> 20:22.451
Hmm...

312
20:23.118 --> 20:26.121
I think you should ask Youjin.

313
20:29.792 --> 20:30.918
Subin.

314
20:32.503 --> 20:33.754
Look at this.

315
20:37.258 --> 20:40.010
He's Youjin's boyfriend.

316
20:41.512 --> 20:42.513
Really?

317
20:42.596 --> 20:43.848
Yeah.

318
20:43.931 --> 20:45.558
That's why she wouldn't tell us.

319
20:45.641 --> 20:48.477
We wanted to thank him, but she said there was no need.

320
20:50.980 --> 20:53.357
Then I don't think it's him.

321
20:53.440 --> 20:54.567
What?

322
20:55.150 --> 20:58.070
That assistant guy has a disability.

323
20:58.571 --> 21:02.533
If he were her boyfriend, she wouldn't have offered to set me up with him.

324
21:02.616 --> 21:03.617
That wouldn't make sense.

325
21:04.827 --> 21:06.036
He's disabled?

326
21:08.622 --> 21:11.208
Uh... I mean...

327
21:12.126 --> 21:17.131
Youjin offered to set me up with him, saying he's a really nice guy.

328
21:17.214 --> 21:19.842
But how could she set you up with someone like that?

329
21:19.925 --> 21:20.926
That's messed up.

330
21:21.010 --> 21:22.177
No, it's not like that.

331
21:22.261 --> 21:25.764
-She said he's a really nice guy. -[chuckles softly]

332
21:25.848 --> 21:28.267
Of course. I feel bad now.

333
21:32.396 --> 21:34.565
So, what's his name?

334
21:35.900 --> 21:37.902
[♪ whimsical music playing]

335
21:55.878 --> 21:58.088
Should we start the meeting now?

336
22:01.133 --> 22:03.719
Chansoo, I can't see the board very well from there.

337
22:03.802 --> 22:04.803
Can I sit here?

338
22:04.887 --> 22:06.388
-Okay, sure. -Thank you.

339
22:11.352 --> 22:12.478
[Choi Hangyeol grunts]

340
22:17.775 --> 22:21.236
[♪ whimsical music continues]

341
22:30.496 --> 22:31.997
Youjin, how are you feeling?

342
22:32.581 --> 22:34.667
I got my stitches out. I'm fine.

343
22:34.750 --> 22:35.751
That's great.

344
22:35.834 --> 22:37.836
Still, you didn't have to come back so soon.

345
22:37.920 --> 22:39.922
You could've taken some more time off.

346
22:40.673 --> 22:42.257
I love coming to school.

347
22:42.341 --> 22:44.259
I always look forward to seeing you guys.

348
22:45.094 --> 22:46.387
But still.

349
22:46.470 --> 22:48.097
Don't push yourself too hard, okay?

350
22:48.180 --> 22:49.723
Work can wait.

351
22:49.807 --> 22:51.976
[Park Minjae] Yeah, you need to take care of yourself.

352
22:52.059 --> 22:53.394
You're an adult.

353
22:53.477 --> 22:54.478
Okay, will do.

354
22:59.692 --> 23:02.444
Did you bring the modeling illustrations you said you'd do?

355
23:03.821 --> 23:06.156
No, I haven't finished yet.

356
23:06.240 --> 23:07.241
Sorry.

357
23:07.324 --> 23:10.285
Hey, you said you'd do it.

358
23:11.370 --> 23:12.705
[Bae Chansoo] She was sick and had surgery.

359
23:12.788 --> 23:14.373
How could she have gotten it done?

360
23:14.873 --> 23:16.792
If she agreed to it, she should've done it.

361
23:16.875 --> 23:18.419
If not, she should've told us.

362
23:18.502 --> 23:23.465
Why don't you just let her handle it and focus on your own work, Sejin?

363
23:23.549 --> 23:25.843
I'm doing my own work just fine.

364
23:26.510 --> 23:27.761
Are you talking back to me?

365
23:27.845 --> 23:29.680
I'm not talking back to you. I'm saying...

366
23:29.763 --> 23:31.348
[Park Minjae] Hey. That's enough, okay?

367
23:31.432 --> 23:34.309
It's not a big deal. Are you really fighting over this?

368
23:34.977 --> 23:36.770
You've gotten a little too comfortable.

369
23:37.855 --> 23:39.940
It's been a while. Want to go back to Dieland?

370
23:40.024 --> 23:41.358
Should I give Seohyun a call?

371
23:41.442 --> 23:42.693
INCOMING CALL CHACHA

372
23:43.360 --> 23:44.695
[cell phone vibrating]

373
23:45.195 --> 23:46.947
The professor was already asking

374
23:47.031 --> 23:50.034
when the upper-body finite element analysis results would be ready.

375
23:50.534 --> 23:52.411
He wanted the results by this afternoon,

376
23:52.995 --> 23:56.331
but we haven't even finished the modeling yet.

377
23:57.666 --> 23:58.792
[cell phone vibrating]

378
23:59.918 --> 24:02.337
INCOMING CALL CHACHA

379
24:02.421 --> 24:04.256
[muttering] Why does she keep calling me?

380
24:04.339 --> 24:07.009
So stop sitting around bickering

381
24:07.092 --> 24:09.344
-and start generating some data. -[cellphone vibrating]

382
24:09.428 --> 24:10.971
You're not undergrads anymore.

383
24:11.055 --> 24:13.265
Do I really have to nag you over basic stuff?

384
24:13.348 --> 24:14.349
[softly] Hello.

385
24:14.433 --> 24:16.101
What are you doing in a meeting?

386
24:17.102 --> 24:18.937
Chacha wants to talk to you.

387
24:19.021 --> 24:20.355
Why did you take that...

388
24:20.439 --> 24:21.440
Hello?

389
24:22.483 --> 24:23.484
[sighs]

390
24:23.567 --> 24:25.027
Huh?

391
24:25.110 --> 24:26.236
What?

392
24:26.320 --> 24:27.780
Friday? What about Friday?

393
24:27.863 --> 24:30.199
You're supposed to go to the musical that day.

394
24:30.282 --> 24:33.160
Those tickets were really hard to get. So don't be late.

395
24:33.243 --> 24:35.454
Look up some good restaurants nearby too.

396
24:36.288 --> 24:38.749
Actually, never mind. I'll do that too.

397
24:38.832 --> 24:40.501
You're clueless about trendy places.

398
24:40.584 --> 24:42.169
I don't care about trendy...

399
24:42.252 --> 24:43.879
I'm busy. I'm in a meeting. Bye.

400
24:44.838 --> 24:45.839
[line disconnects]

401
24:46.715 --> 24:48.634
Minjae, is that about the blind date?

402
24:48.717 --> 24:49.718
Right?

403
24:50.427 --> 24:51.845
You should go for it.

404
24:51.929 --> 24:55.599
She looked pretty in that picture, and you two looked good together.

405
24:57.101 --> 24:58.727
That's not true.

406
24:58.811 --> 25:01.021
Anyway, enough about that. Where were we?

407
25:01.855 --> 25:03.941
-Huh? -We hadn't really gotten anywhere yet.

408
25:04.858 --> 25:05.943
No, wait.

409
25:06.443 --> 25:09.196
Yeah. How far have we gotten with the modeling illustrations?

410
25:09.279 --> 25:10.864
Lim Youjin didn't do it.

411
25:11.657 --> 25:12.658
Youjin...

412
25:16.370 --> 25:17.955
[sighs softly]

413
25:35.264 --> 25:36.682
[cellphone vibrating]

414
25:38.308 --> 25:39.309
Yeah.

415
25:40.144 --> 25:42.229
I just stepped out. I'm on a coffee run.

416
25:43.689 --> 25:46.024
I have to feed them to get their brains going.

417
25:48.277 --> 25:49.278
What?

418
25:49.987 --> 25:50.988
Why?

419
25:52.406 --> 25:55.200
Come on, you have to go on three dates before you can tell.

420
25:56.451 --> 25:57.452
[yells] Hey!

421
26:01.331 --> 26:04.209
[softly] You think you're the only one who's busy? We're all busy.

422
26:05.210 --> 26:08.130
Park Minjae, you're not seeing someone, are you?

423
26:08.714 --> 26:11.133
What are you talking about? I'm not seeing anyone.

424
26:11.967 --> 26:13.051
Well,

425
26:14.136 --> 26:16.972
it's not like I'm anything special

426
26:17.681 --> 26:19.892
or have much more to offer than other people.

427
26:21.393 --> 26:22.436
And honestly...

428
26:23.520 --> 26:27.107
uh... I don't even know if I'm qualified.

429
26:27.691 --> 26:29.735
Qualified? Qualified for what?

430
26:31.195 --> 26:33.197
You say the weirdest things sometimes.

431
26:34.114 --> 26:35.115
I mean, sure,

432
26:35.908 --> 26:38.160
your personality isn't exactly your strong suit.

433
26:38.243 --> 26:40.662
You overthink everything, and you're stubborn.

434
26:42.289 --> 26:44.541
But who dates for personality these days?

435
26:44.625 --> 26:45.709
It's all about looks.

436
26:47.586 --> 26:49.713
And you're pretty good-looking.

437
26:50.422 --> 26:51.423
Yeah?

438
26:52.299 --> 26:53.300
I am?

439
26:53.967 --> 26:54.968
[knock at door]

440
26:55.052 --> 26:56.595
Someone's here. I have to go.

441
26:56.678 --> 26:57.679
Bye.

442
26:58.347 --> 26:59.348
[line disconnects]

443
26:59.431 --> 27:01.308
-Yes? -[door opens]

444
27:04.144 --> 27:05.187
How can I help you?

445
27:05.687 --> 27:10.442
Uh, hi. Do you know someone named Lim Youjin in this lab?

446
27:11.944 --> 27:12.945
Who are you?

447
27:13.946 --> 27:16.365
Hello, my name is Lim Youseong.

448
27:16.448 --> 27:17.950
I'm Youjin's older brother.

449
27:18.033 --> 27:19.034
[dramatic sting]

450
27:19.117 --> 27:20.869
[hesitating] I see. Okay.

451
27:23.121 --> 27:24.414
[Choi Hangyeol] Let's move it forward first.

452
27:24.498 --> 27:25.499
-[Eom Taeho] Okay. -[Choi Hangyeol] Move forward.

453
27:25.582 --> 27:27.960
[♪ upbeat music playing]

454
27:30.337 --> 27:31.421
Hangyeol.

455
27:33.131 --> 27:34.216
Try moving it backward.

456
27:34.299 --> 27:35.801
Backward? Okay, moving backward.

457
27:42.099 --> 27:43.141
-[cellphone vibrating] -Oh?

458
27:43.225 --> 27:44.935
Sorry, excuse me for a moment.

459
27:46.561 --> 27:48.063
Subin, I'll call you back.

460
27:50.482 --> 27:51.483
What?

461
27:51.566 --> 27:52.985
My brother?

462
27:54.111 --> 27:55.112
When?

463
27:55.737 --> 27:56.738
Yeah.

464
27:57.364 --> 27:58.365
Yeah.

465
28:00.075 --> 28:01.076
What?

466
28:01.868 --> 28:04.287
What a nut. Seriously, has he lost his mind?

467
28:05.372 --> 28:07.124
Okay, just hang up for now.

468
28:08.917 --> 28:12.170
I'm so sorry, but something came up. I need to step out for a minute.

469
28:12.254 --> 28:13.964
-Hey! -I promise. Just a sec.

470
28:14.047 --> 28:15.048
Hey!

471
28:15.716 --> 28:16.925
[Kang Miran] What's wrong?

472
28:19.511 --> 28:21.763
Maybe I shouldn't have told her brother about it.

473
28:22.264 --> 28:26.018
What brother would be happy to hear that his sister's boyfriend is disabled?

474
28:26.101 --> 28:27.102
They'd be shocked.

475
28:28.103 --> 28:29.688
He's not her boyfriend.

476
28:30.605 --> 28:31.773
He's not.

477
28:32.357 --> 28:34.443
Then things should get cleared up soon.

478
28:40.741 --> 28:41.908
Wait.

479
28:42.409 --> 28:44.911
Could that research assistant be into Youjin?

480
29:07.684 --> 29:10.562
This is all I have to offer right now.

481
29:10.645 --> 29:11.646
I'm sorry.

482
29:11.772 --> 29:14.191
No. This is great.

483
29:14.274 --> 29:15.275
Okay.

484
29:18.111 --> 29:19.196
So...

485
29:20.030 --> 29:24.117
Should I try giving Ms. Lim Youjin a call?

486
29:24.201 --> 29:25.786
No. Forget about Youjin.

487
29:26.453 --> 29:30.457
To tell you the truth, I'm here to see you, Mr. Park Minjae.

488
29:31.249 --> 29:32.334
Me?

489
29:33.210 --> 29:34.961
But sir, why would you...

490
29:35.045 --> 29:36.671
Don't call me sir.

491
29:36.755 --> 29:38.256
I'm just Youjin's brother.

492
29:39.049 --> 29:41.176
Right, her brother. Right.

493
29:41.259 --> 29:44.221
So, as her brother, why did you want to see me?

494
29:44.304 --> 29:46.890
It's nothing much.

495
29:46.973 --> 29:50.268
I've basically left her here without ever properly introducing myself,

496
29:50.352 --> 29:52.979
-so figured I'd stop by while I was here. -Ah!

497
29:53.105 --> 29:55.857
Thank you for always looking out for her. I owe you so much.

498
29:55.941 --> 29:57.275
Not at all.

499
29:57.359 --> 30:00.946
Ms. Lim Youjin is really kind and hardworking.

500
30:01.029 --> 30:04.074
She's absolutely indispensable to our lab.

501
30:04.157 --> 30:06.159
A truly exceptional researcher, yes.

502
30:06.701 --> 30:08.703
The professors speak very highly of her too.

503
30:08.787 --> 30:10.539
-Really? -Yes.

504
30:10.622 --> 30:12.958
I'm glad to hear that they think so highly of her.

505
30:19.506 --> 30:21.466
Should I give Youjin a call?

506
30:21.550 --> 30:23.844
No. I actually came here because...

507
30:23.927 --> 30:24.928
Yes?

508
30:25.846 --> 30:28.265
There's something I wanted to ask you.

509
30:28.348 --> 30:30.475
Sure, what is it?

510
30:30.559 --> 30:32.853
When Youjin had appendicitis the other day...

511
30:32.936 --> 30:34.229
Yes.

512
30:34.312 --> 30:38.066
I heard a male professor here took her to the hospital.

513
30:38.150 --> 30:40.152
I was wondering if you might know who it was.

514
30:41.778 --> 30:42.779
A professor?

515
30:42.863 --> 30:45.699
Yes. I hear he's really tall and handsome.

516
30:45.782 --> 30:48.618
He's a male professor in his early to mid-30s.

517
30:49.578 --> 30:51.580
Is there a professor that young?

518
30:51.663 --> 30:54.624
[muttering]

519
30:54.708 --> 30:56.543
Well, I'm not sure.

520
30:57.335 --> 31:01.214
I'd really like to meet him and say thank you.

521
31:01.298 --> 31:02.507
Oh.

522
31:02.591 --> 31:03.800
Do you know who he is?

523
31:03.884 --> 31:06.803
No, I've never heard about this.

524
31:07.637 --> 31:08.763
Uh...

525
31:09.306 --> 31:11.725
Why don't you ask Youjin yourself?

526
31:11.808 --> 31:13.810
I did, but she wouldn't tell me.

527
31:13.894 --> 31:15.478
She's keeping it to herself.

528
31:16.771 --> 31:17.772
Why?

529
31:17.856 --> 31:20.108
I don't know why she'd keep it to herself.

530
31:22.485 --> 31:23.904
You really don't know?

531
31:23.987 --> 31:26.573
No, this is the first time I've heard about it.

532
31:29.868 --> 31:31.077
Then...

533
31:34.581 --> 31:36.333
Have you seen something like this?

534
31:37.042 --> 31:39.502
What... is this?

535
31:40.587 --> 31:42.172
Youseong, It's not him.

536
31:42.297 --> 31:44.549
It's... It's someone else. There's someone else.

537
31:45.050 --> 31:47.802
I'll take you to meet him. Come on out.

538
31:47.886 --> 31:49.888
I'm just having some coffee. What's up?

539
31:49.971 --> 31:52.891
You win, okay? I'm sorry. Now, hurry up and come on out.

540
31:52.974 --> 31:54.059
What... Hey.

541
31:54.142 --> 31:56.436
Hey, wait. I need to say goodbye, you know.

542
31:56.519 --> 31:57.604
I'll see you next time.

543
31:57.687 --> 31:59.397
-Okay. Take care. -Come on.

544
31:59.481 --> 32:01.191
What kind of research do you do here?

545
32:07.697 --> 32:08.865
[Lim Youseong] Hey, let go of me.

546
32:08.949 --> 32:10.742
-Let go of me! -Could you just...

547
32:10.825 --> 32:12.285
You're hurting my arm, you brat.

548
32:12.369 --> 32:13.536
-Let go. -Gosh.

549
32:14.955 --> 32:15.956
Seriously.

550
32:16.623 --> 32:18.250
So why did you cross the line?

551
32:18.792 --> 32:20.752
You crossed the line first, you know?

552
32:21.378 --> 32:23.380
You're the one who started this. Okay?

553
32:28.260 --> 32:29.261
[sighs]

554
32:33.974 --> 32:36.476
[Lim Youseong] I should've stopped by to introduce myself sooner.

555
32:37.394 --> 32:40.063
Nice to meet you. I'm Lim Youseong, Youjin's older brother.

556
32:40.647 --> 32:41.648
I'm Lee Jihoon.

557
32:41.731 --> 32:42.732
Oh.

558
32:42.816 --> 32:46.736
I heard things could've gone really bad if it hadn't been for you.

559
32:48.029 --> 32:49.030
Thank you so much.

560
32:49.114 --> 32:50.407
You saved her life.

561
32:50.490 --> 32:51.491
Not at all.

562
32:51.574 --> 32:54.202
I just happened to come across her and took her to the hospital.

563
32:54.911 --> 32:58.039
By the way, you're really young for a math professor.

564
32:58.957 --> 32:59.958
Wow.

565
33:00.041 --> 33:01.167
Are you married, by any chance?

566
33:01.835 --> 33:03.336
Uh, no, not yet.

567
33:03.420 --> 33:04.963
I see. You're not.

568
33:05.630 --> 33:07.132
What about a girlfriend?

569
33:07.215 --> 33:09.134
Stop. You're being rude, Youseong.

570
33:09.217 --> 33:10.677
Nothing's going on with you two?

571
33:10.760 --> 33:11.886
Oh.

572
33:12.595 --> 33:14.931
I'm her professor, and she's my student.

573
33:15.807 --> 33:19.602
Or we might be a hat and a monkey.

574
33:20.770 --> 33:22.814
-Pardon? -No, it's nothing.

575
33:25.984 --> 33:27.110
Hold on a second.

576
33:29.863 --> 33:31.740
Have you seen these rings before?

577
33:34.117 --> 33:35.118
[Lee Jihoon] Hmm...

578
33:36.536 --> 33:37.746
No, I've never seen them.

579
33:40.498 --> 33:41.708
Okay. Well...

580
33:45.712 --> 33:46.713
[mouthing] That's twice.

581
33:54.429 --> 33:57.015
It was wrong of me to bring Jihye up.

582
33:57.098 --> 33:58.099
I apologize.

583
34:00.894 --> 34:04.189
[sighs] But you came all the way to my school and humiliated me.

584
34:04.272 --> 34:05.982
Haven't you gotten back at me enough?

585
34:06.066 --> 34:08.860
Hey, how is that humiliating?

586
34:08.943 --> 34:11.029
I just went there as your brother to say hello

587
34:11.112 --> 34:13.239
and ask them to look out for you, you brat.

588
34:19.704 --> 34:20.997
I won't tell Mom.

589
34:21.748 --> 34:23.124
She'd kill you.

590
34:23.208 --> 34:24.209
[in English] Thank you.

591
34:25.377 --> 34:26.628
So we're good now?

592
34:27.295 --> 34:29.839
[in Korean] From now on, you show me some respect, okay?

593
34:31.674 --> 34:32.884
We'll see.

594
34:33.885 --> 34:34.886
Now go.

595
34:38.640 --> 34:40.058
[car engine starts]

596
34:52.612 --> 34:54.614
[♪ pensive music playing]

597
35:50.670 --> 35:51.671
Yeah.

598
35:51.963 --> 35:53.047
Good. Great job.

599
35:54.007 --> 35:57.844
Once you organize the data a little better, it should pass review.

600
35:58.845 --> 36:03.641
We need to emphasize the study's contributions beyond existing research.

601
36:03.725 --> 36:07.395
If you can articulate that well, I think we'll be fine.

602
36:07.896 --> 36:08.897
Yes, understood.

603
36:10.273 --> 36:11.483
And what are your plans?

604
36:13.443 --> 36:15.236
You're getting your PhD this year.

605
36:15.320 --> 36:17.530
-Have you thought about doing a postdoc? -Ah.

606
36:18.281 --> 36:19.282
Yes.

607
36:20.950 --> 36:23.161
You did both your master's and PhD here in Korea.

608
36:23.995 --> 36:27.207
You should go abroad for your postdoc.

609
36:27.290 --> 36:31.503
Yes, actually, I've been looking into programs in the US and Australia.

610
36:32.295 --> 36:34.798
I hear there's an opening at Stanford.

611
36:37.467 --> 36:41.888
Mm. I put in a good word for you, so feel free to reach out if you're interested.

612
36:42.847 --> 36:44.849
Sure. Thank you.

613
36:45.350 --> 36:47.602
If it works out, you owe me dinner, okay?

614
36:47.685 --> 36:49.312
Of course.

615
36:50.563 --> 36:51.564
[knock at door]

616
36:51.648 --> 36:52.774
-Yes? -Yes?

617
36:54.442 --> 36:56.778
-It's you. -Hi, Sejin. Come on in.

618
36:57.362 --> 36:58.446
Here, have a seat.

619
37:00.406 --> 37:03.701
I heard things are a mess in Professor Hwang's lab at KAIST.

620
37:04.702 --> 37:06.955
They've had three researchers leave,

621
37:07.038 --> 37:09.749
and now all their project bids are getting pushed back.

622
37:10.542 --> 37:13.211
They might not even be able to participate in the WRS.

623
37:13.294 --> 37:14.295
Is that true?

624
37:15.880 --> 37:16.923
Yeah, I guess.

625
37:17.006 --> 37:18.842
Wait, Professor Hwang's lab?

626
37:18.925 --> 37:20.927
-Was there an accident? -Yeah, apparently.

627
37:21.719 --> 37:22.720
What accident?

628
37:23.346 --> 37:26.850
Well, it's not a lab accident.

629
37:26.933 --> 37:27.934
Yeah.

630
37:28.017 --> 37:29.018
[sighs]

631
37:30.603 --> 37:32.564
There was drama. Relationship drama.

632
37:32.647 --> 37:33.982
Relationship drama?

633
37:34.065 --> 37:36.484
There was this couple in the lab,

634
37:37.110 --> 37:38.528
and one of them was two-timing.

635
37:39.153 --> 37:40.530
Oh!

636
37:40.613 --> 37:43.324
So all three people in the love triangle quit,

637
37:43.408 --> 37:46.744
and the friends they hung out with started taking sides and fighting too.

638
37:47.745 --> 37:49.455
-It turned into a complete mess. -Yes.

639
37:49.539 --> 37:50.540
I see.

640
37:50.623 --> 37:52.584
Well, with so many young, single people around,

641
37:52.667 --> 37:54.878
-I guess these things happen. -Mm.

642
37:55.795 --> 37:58.214
Maybe it's time we instituted

643
37:59.257 --> 38:02.343
a no-dating policy in our lab too? [chuckles]

644
38:02.427 --> 38:03.761
-A no-dating policy? -Yeah.

645
38:09.058 --> 38:12.145
You've been here a little while. Are you settling in okay?

646
38:13.021 --> 38:15.523
When it comes to settling in, honestly...

647
38:16.190 --> 38:17.191
[Park Minjae] Hmm?

648
38:17.275 --> 38:19.360
I'd heard this was basically a free-range lab,

649
38:19.444 --> 38:21.195
but it's even worse than I thought.

650
38:23.656 --> 38:28.036
I mean, the autonomy is nice, but it might be a little too loose here.

651
38:28.119 --> 38:29.120
Hmm.

652
38:29.203 --> 38:34.000
Especially when romance is involved, things can get really messy in a lab.

653
38:35.877 --> 38:37.462
[sighing] But don't worry.

654
38:37.545 --> 38:39.923
You've got me here.

655
38:40.840 --> 38:43.384
I have a hypothesis. All I need to do is prove it.

656
38:43.468 --> 38:46.304
I'll nip this in the bud before it causes any trouble.

657
38:46.387 --> 38:47.388
Okay.

658
38:48.056 --> 38:50.725
Even if you go to the States, I'll hold down the fort here.

659
38:50.808 --> 38:51.809
So don't worry.

660
38:53.895 --> 38:55.104
Hey, wait.

661
38:56.189 --> 38:57.607
How did you know about that?

662
38:58.816 --> 38:59.817
What?

663
39:00.777 --> 39:02.487
I just heard about it.

664
39:02.570 --> 39:03.571
You...

665
39:04.197 --> 39:06.532
Nothing's been decided. I don't know yet.

666
39:07.909 --> 39:09.661
But the professor said it was all set.

667
39:09.744 --> 39:12.455
No way. There's still a long way to go.

668
39:13.665 --> 39:15.124
[sighs]

669
39:16.709 --> 39:19.712
-Don't tell the other guys about it, okay? -Okay.

670
39:19.796 --> 39:20.797
[automated voice] Fifth floor.

671
39:25.176 --> 39:26.177
Going down.

672
39:27.679 --> 39:28.680
-Don't. -Okay.

673
39:54.998 --> 39:57.000
[♪ pleasant music playing]

674
39:57.083 --> 39:58.084
[keyboard clacking]

675
40:15.393 --> 40:16.602
[sighs]

676
40:20.690 --> 40:22.358
-[Park Minjae] Lim Youjin. -Yes?

677
40:22.442 --> 40:24.527
How's the modeling illustration coming along?

678
40:25.778 --> 40:27.697
Oh, I'm working on it now.

679
40:27.780 --> 40:29.240
Can you finish it by today?

680
40:29.323 --> 40:30.742
Today? No.

681
40:33.703 --> 40:35.621
Can you finish it by the end of this week?

682
40:35.705 --> 40:37.498
Yeah, I can finish it by then.

683
40:38.082 --> 40:40.418
Let's pick up the pace and make up for the delay.

684
40:41.127 --> 40:42.211
Okay.

685
40:48.384 --> 40:50.636
Okay, I'm heading out for the day.

686
40:50.720 --> 40:53.181
You guys can leave whenever you're done.

687
40:53.264 --> 40:54.265
-Okay. -Okay.

688
41:00.521 --> 41:02.148
Hey, Lim Youjin.

689
41:02.231 --> 41:03.941
Finish that before you leave.

690
41:11.783 --> 41:15.328
[♪ pleasant music continues]

691
41:33.971 --> 41:35.098
Aren't you going home?

692
41:36.057 --> 41:37.141
[scoffs]

693
41:37.225 --> 41:38.726
I'm just going to finish this up.

694
41:39.769 --> 41:41.395
[Kim Sejin] Okay. Good luck.

695
41:46.025 --> 41:47.026
[door opens]

696
41:49.070 --> 41:50.071
[door closes]

697
42:17.849 --> 42:20.977
Lim Youjin. Why are you coming out so late?

698
42:21.060 --> 42:22.353
Do you know what time it is?

699
42:22.436 --> 42:24.522
Weren't you even hungry? Huh?

700
42:26.524 --> 42:27.525
I'm hungry.

701
42:28.609 --> 42:29.610
Me too.

702
42:36.159 --> 42:38.452
-Slow down. Take your time. -[sighs]

703
42:38.536 --> 42:40.163
Why haven't you eaten yet?

704
42:41.122 --> 42:42.790
You haven't even fully recovered.

705
42:43.749 --> 42:45.459
Because I had some work to finish.

706
42:46.669 --> 42:48.838
It's because of Kim Sejin, that jerk, wasn't it?

707
42:49.922 --> 42:51.424
No.

708
42:51.507 --> 42:52.717
It wasn't Kim Sejin.

709
42:53.634 --> 42:55.094
It was Park Minjae.

710
42:56.888 --> 42:57.889
Hmm.

711
43:02.685 --> 43:04.562
Want me to order something else?

712
43:04.645 --> 43:06.856
-No. -Do you want some sushi?

713
43:07.899 --> 43:10.735
No, my stomach would burst. Then I'd need surgery again.

714
43:15.406 --> 43:17.450
Were you surprised today?

715
43:18.201 --> 43:20.578
-Hmm? -Because of my brother.

716
43:22.288 --> 43:23.289
No.

717
43:24.207 --> 43:28.169
He just wanted to see the lab and say hello.

718
43:28.669 --> 43:29.879
He won't be coming back.

719
43:32.798 --> 43:36.552
Right, who's that person who took you to the hospital?

720
43:36.636 --> 43:37.637
A professor?

721
43:38.221 --> 43:41.557
Yeah. Professor Lee Jihoon. Professor Talking Hat.

722
43:41.641 --> 43:42.642
Oh.

723
43:43.851 --> 43:46.062
But why didn't you tell me?

724
43:48.898 --> 43:50.816
I didn't because you never asked.

725
43:52.652 --> 43:54.278
I didn't ask because I didn't know.

726
43:57.990 --> 44:00.952
Wait, are you... jealous?

727
44:01.035 --> 44:02.036
Hmm?

728
44:04.664 --> 44:05.665
You are.

729
44:05.748 --> 44:07.250
You are jealous.

730
44:07.917 --> 44:08.918
[scoffs]

731
44:09.001 --> 44:11.671
What are you talking about? Why would I be jealous? No way.

732
44:13.714 --> 44:15.633
You know, if...

733
44:16.384 --> 44:20.137
if you go see a musical or a movie with some other woman,

734
44:20.221 --> 44:21.806
it doesn't bother me at all.

735
44:26.143 --> 44:28.771
[sighing]

736
44:30.940 --> 44:33.150
What do you want to do after this?

737
44:33.818 --> 44:35.945
-Hmm? -Should we go to your place?

738
44:37.488 --> 44:39.740
Uh... we can't.

739
44:40.324 --> 44:41.367
Why not?

740
44:41.450 --> 44:43.828
Kim Sejin is watching.

741
44:58.801 --> 45:01.762
[sighs heavily]

742
45:01.846 --> 45:03.597
Do you want to sit here for a bit?

743
45:22.199 --> 45:24.827
Wearing your prosthetic leg all day must hurt a lot.

744
45:25.703 --> 45:28.622
No, I'm used to it now, so it's fine.

745
45:34.211 --> 45:36.464
I'll be good to you from now on.

746
45:40.051 --> 45:41.302
I'll be good to you.

747
45:45.514 --> 45:48.684
Are you going to meet that woman from the blind date again?

748
45:52.480 --> 45:54.482
Are you going to meet her again?

749
45:59.403 --> 46:00.404
I'm not.

750
46:03.741 --> 46:04.742
[Lim Youjin] Hmm.

751
46:04.825 --> 46:08.037
Once I get my PhD, I need to go to the States for my postdoc,

752
46:08.120 --> 46:10.122
so I can't really start seeing anyone right now.

753
46:24.178 --> 46:25.596
When would you be going?

754
46:26.680 --> 46:27.681
Uh...

755
46:28.849 --> 46:30.518
I'll be getting my degree this year,

756
46:30.601 --> 46:33.437
so maybe toward the end of this year or sometime next year?

757
46:34.772 --> 46:35.773
Hmm.

758
46:35.856 --> 46:37.274
When would you come back?

759
46:37.942 --> 46:39.610
Two years at the earliest.

760
46:40.236 --> 46:42.238
It could be several years, though.

761
46:46.992 --> 46:48.119
But...

762
46:49.245 --> 46:51.122
it's not like you're never coming back.

763
46:51.205 --> 46:52.706
I might never come back.

764
46:57.211 --> 46:58.421
I won't come back.

765
47:12.560 --> 47:15.104
I should've told you sooner. I'm sorry.

766
47:20.526 --> 47:21.527
Hmm.

767
47:23.404 --> 47:24.780
So you're turning me down?

768
47:27.366 --> 47:29.201
You're saying you can't date me.

769
47:30.202 --> 47:32.079
You're turning me down.

770
47:34.248 --> 47:35.249
I'm sorry.

771
47:36.876 --> 47:39.795
[sighs heavily]

772
47:40.212 --> 47:45.050
It's kind of stupid to be turned down twice by the same man.

773
47:46.594 --> 47:48.304
But what can I do?

774
47:50.973 --> 47:52.475
That's for me to deal with,

775
47:53.517 --> 47:55.478
and you have your own things to deal with.

776
48:03.110 --> 48:04.111
But...

777
48:05.154 --> 48:07.656
I thought you liked me at least a little.

778
48:12.661 --> 48:14.580
Don't be so nice to me anymore.

779
48:14.663 --> 48:16.040
It gives me the wrong idea.

780
48:16.123 --> 48:18.125
[♪ melancholy song playing]

781
48:39.063 --> 48:40.064
[Lim Youseong] Is that you, Youjin?

782
48:40.731 --> 48:42.024
Yeah.

783
48:42.107 --> 48:45.277
Do you know what time it is? You should try to get home earlier.

784
48:45.361 --> 48:46.529
Okay.

785
48:46.612 --> 48:47.613
Lim Youjin.

786
48:50.699 --> 48:54.620
You know how much Mom and Dad love you, right?

787
48:56.330 --> 48:57.331
What?

788
48:58.749 --> 49:00.960
Don't you ever let them down.

789
49:04.171 --> 49:05.172
Okay.

790
49:06.632 --> 49:08.801
[door lock beeps]

791
49:33.701 --> 49:34.702
[sighs softly]

792
49:44.336 --> 49:45.337
[sighs heavily]

793
49:48.340 --> 49:49.341
[sighs heavily]

794
49:51.385 --> 49:52.386
[sniffles]

795
49:53.429 --> 49:54.513
[breath trembling]

796
50:01.395 --> 50:03.564
[sobbing]

797
50:06.525 --> 50:07.735
[door lock chimes]

798
50:14.617 --> 50:15.618
[door beeps]

799
50:19.246 --> 50:20.247
[sighs softly]

800
50:42.061 --> 50:43.062
[sighs softly]

801
51:26.522 --> 51:27.815
[exhales sharply]

802
51:31.819 --> 51:32.820
[music ends]

803
51:39.159 --> 51:42.830
ENGINEERING BUILDING 3

804
51:44.331 --> 51:45.332
Good morning.

805
51:46.333 --> 51:48.794
[Kim Sejin] It's a 90-millimeter refractor telescope.

806
51:48.877 --> 51:49.878
What are you doing?

807
51:49.962 --> 51:52.089
-You can see the details on the moon. -Minjae.

808
51:52.172 --> 51:53.424
Sejin bought a telescope.

809
51:53.507 --> 51:55.467
-Hey, you're shaking it. -Is it working?

810
51:55.551 --> 51:57.261
Why did you suddenly buy a telescope?

811
51:58.011 --> 52:00.431
-It's just a hobby. -Oh.

812
52:00.514 --> 52:02.975
I heard there's going to be a solar eclipse here soon.

813
52:03.058 --> 52:04.059
A solar eclipse?

814
52:04.143 --> 52:05.394
-A solar eclipse? -When?

815
52:05.477 --> 52:07.479
There's a partial solar eclipse in 2030.

816
52:07.896 --> 52:09.481
-[Eom Taeho] Hmm. -In 2030?

817
52:10.274 --> 52:12.025
-That's a long way off. -Still far off.

818
52:12.109 --> 52:15.571
Well, I thought I could practice

819
52:15.654 --> 52:18.157
taking pictures with it between now and then.

820
52:18.907 --> 52:19.992
All right.

821
52:20.075 --> 52:23.245
I heard the Aris meteor shower peaks early Saturday morning.

822
52:23.328 --> 52:24.496
We could watch that.

823
52:24.913 --> 52:26.373
-What? A meteor shower? -[Eom Taeho] Oh!

824
52:26.457 --> 52:28.125
Cool. I've only seen it in movies.

825
52:28.208 --> 52:31.712
Where you wish on shooting stars, right? I saw it on TV.

826
52:31.795 --> 52:33.547
We don't have to go to an observatory.

827
52:33.630 --> 52:35.340
We can watch it from Sejin's place.

828
52:35.424 --> 52:37.885
Yeah. That could be your housewarming party too, right?

829
52:37.968 --> 52:40.471
Stargazing and drinks on the rooftop?

830
52:40.554 --> 52:42.890
-Damn, it'll be romantic as hell. -[Bae Chansoo] Oh.

831
52:42.973 --> 52:45.350
For stargazing, the weather matters a lot.

832
52:45.434 --> 52:46.435
What's the forecast?

833
52:46.518 --> 52:49.146
It's supposed to be clear. Perfect weather for stargazing.

834
52:49.730 --> 52:52.232
Well, my place is kind of small, though.

835
52:53.734 --> 52:57.070
It doesn't matter. We'll be on the rooftop to watch the stars anyway.

836
52:57.154 --> 52:58.489
We'll grill up there too.

837
52:58.572 --> 53:00.866
Right. We need a picnic blanket too, right?

838
53:01.575 --> 53:03.160
And a gas burner for the barbecue.

839
53:03.243 --> 53:05.871
Oh? That sounds great. I'm excited.

840
53:05.954 --> 53:07.664
[giggling]

841
53:11.502 --> 53:12.753
You're coming too, right?

842
53:12.836 --> 53:13.837
What?

843
53:13.921 --> 53:15.172
You should come too.

844
53:15.255 --> 53:18.175
No, I'm behind on 10 papers to review.

845
53:18.258 --> 53:19.718
You guys go have fun without me.

846
53:19.802 --> 53:23.764
Come on, Minjae, you've got to have some fun once in a while.

847
53:23.847 --> 53:26.475
He's busy with his studies. Let's hang out by ourselves.

848
53:26.558 --> 53:27.559
Maybe you're right.

849
53:27.643 --> 53:28.644
Okay, then.

850
53:40.280 --> 53:41.365
[groans softly]

851
53:45.702 --> 53:47.037
[grunts]

852
54:03.262 --> 54:05.430
[breathing heavily]

853
54:06.473 --> 54:08.851
[distant laughter]

854
54:08.934 --> 54:10.936
[♪ pleasant music playing]

855
54:16.567 --> 54:17.568
[Eom Taeho] Oh!

856
54:17.651 --> 54:19.570
I can see it! [laughs excitedly]

857
54:20.153 --> 54:21.780
I can see the moon! [gasps]

858
54:21.864 --> 54:24.491
-Wow! It's so big. -[Choi Hangyeol] What else can you see?

859
54:24.575 --> 54:26.326
[Eom Taeho laughing]

860
54:26.410 --> 54:28.245
The moon... Let me see.

861
54:28.328 --> 54:31.331
The moon, the moon...

862
54:32.916 --> 54:34.001
is the only thing I see.

863
54:34.084 --> 54:35.294
There are too many clouds.

864
54:35.377 --> 54:36.378
Can I take a look too?

865
54:36.461 --> 54:39.339
Well, the meteor shower is supposed to peak between 1:00 and 2:00,

866
54:39.423 --> 54:40.924
so it should clear up by then.

867
54:41.675 --> 54:42.676
Huh? Hey.

868
54:42.759 --> 54:44.177
Hey, let me take a look too.

869
54:45.929 --> 54:48.432
The meat is burning. Guys, come over here and eat.

870
54:48.515 --> 54:49.516
[Eom Taeho] Okay.

871
54:50.100 --> 54:51.268
[Bae Chansoo] It looks a bit different.

872
54:52.060 --> 54:53.437
[Eom Taeho] Oh, oh.

873
54:53.520 --> 54:54.855
Okay.

874
54:54.938 --> 54:56.315
Let me move the plates.

875
54:58.734 --> 55:02.070
Youjin, you're even good at grilling, huh?

876
55:02.154 --> 55:04.156
-[Lim Youjin laughs] -[Choi Hangyeol] Where's the kimchi?

877
55:04.239 --> 55:06.533
-Kimchi. -Kimchi.

878
55:06.617 --> 55:07.618
[Eom Taeho] Thank you.

879
55:07.701 --> 55:08.827
It looks so delicious.

880
55:08.910 --> 55:10.621
Why, thank you.

881
55:10.704 --> 55:12.789
We should've grilled some kimchi too.

882
55:12.873 --> 55:14.041
[Lim Youjin] Should I grill some?

883
55:14.124 --> 55:15.500
[Eom Taeho] No, let's eat this first.

884
55:15.584 --> 55:16.710
[Lim Youjin] Okay, I'll do it after I eat.

885
55:16.793 --> 55:19.588
[♪ melancholy music playing]

886
55:35.771 --> 55:36.855
[gasps]

887
55:39.316 --> 55:40.359
Busted.

888
55:40.442 --> 55:41.777
-Busted. -[Lim Youjin] You have to drink.

889
55:41.860 --> 55:43.028
-Drink. -Drink.

890
55:43.111 --> 55:44.696
Why do you guys keep targeting me?

891
55:44.780 --> 55:49.368
[all chanting] Drink!

892
55:49.951 --> 55:51.036
Drink!

893
55:52.412 --> 55:54.206
-[Eom Taeho] Bottoms up. -[Bae Chansoo] You've got to chug it.

894
55:55.082 --> 55:57.459
[all exclaiming]

895
55:57.542 --> 55:59.044
[laughing]

896
55:59.711 --> 56:01.296
-[Lim Youjin] He's good. -Man, he's good.

897
56:01.380 --> 56:02.673
He's knocking it back.

898
56:06.635 --> 56:07.844
[Bae Chansoo] Man, he sure can drink.

899
56:08.345 --> 56:09.554
[Lim Youjin sighing]

900
56:09.638 --> 56:10.639
Wait, what?

901
56:10.722 --> 56:13.016
-[Eom Taeho] Are we out? -No more drinks?

902
56:13.100 --> 56:14.393
I'll go get some more.

903
56:14.476 --> 56:16.103
-No, I'll go get it. -No.

904
56:16.186 --> 56:18.814
Come on. I'm the youngest. I'll be right back.

905
56:18.897 --> 56:21.233
Wait, but...

906
56:38.959 --> 56:40.460
[door bell tinkles]

907
56:40.544 --> 56:42.254
[thunder rumbling]

908
56:47.509 --> 56:48.969
[rain pattering]

909
56:49.052 --> 56:50.053
Huh?

910
56:50.137 --> 56:52.139
[♪ theme song playing]

911
57:22.210 --> 57:23.712
Taeho, it's raining.

912
57:25.213 --> 57:26.214
Hey.

913
57:26.298 --> 57:27.299
Hey!

914
57:28.258 --> 57:29.718
Hey, wake up, wake up.

915
57:29.843 --> 57:32.721
Wake up.

916
57:32.804 --> 57:34.389
Let's get inside.

917
57:34.473 --> 57:36.558
Is it okay for this to get wet? Come on.

918
57:36.641 --> 57:37.642
[stutters]

919
57:37.726 --> 57:40.520
Hey, make sure to bring that in.

920
57:40.604 --> 57:44.065
Right, the power. We need to unplug it. This...

921
57:45.275 --> 57:46.359
Hey, the cord, quick.

922
57:47.194 --> 57:48.487
Chansoo.

923
57:48.570 --> 57:49.780
Let me take this in.

924
57:49.863 --> 57:52.949
[♪ theme song continues]

925
58:08.799 --> 58:10.258
[thunder rumbling]

926
58:19.601 --> 58:21.394
[thunder rumbling]

927
58:49.923 --> 58:51.091
[grunts]

928
58:54.553 --> 58:55.637
[music ends]

929
58:55.720 --> 58:58.098
What the... Come in.

930
59:00.934 --> 59:02.102
[chuckles]

931
59:02.185 --> 59:04.729
Hey, you can't just bring it here without telling them.

932
59:04.813 --> 59:06.731
It's fine. They don't know it was me.

933
59:07.899 --> 59:09.943
It's raining, and he doesn't have his camera.

934
59:10.026 --> 59:11.111
He'll never find out.

935
59:11.945 --> 59:13.780
Besides, I've got an alibi.

936
59:14.406 --> 59:16.366
You'll be my alibi, right?

937
59:16.449 --> 59:17.450
No.

938
59:19.452 --> 59:21.037
Solar eclipse, my foot.

939
59:21.121 --> 59:24.040
He bought it to spy on your house.

940
59:26.877 --> 59:28.336
No way.

941
59:29.796 --> 59:31.798
If he did, he's a totally crazy pervert.

942
59:32.507 --> 59:34.301
He is a totally crazy pervert.

943
59:36.386 --> 59:37.762
No, he isn't.

944
59:41.308 --> 59:44.394
You don't have to worry about anything anymore.

945
59:46.062 --> 59:47.147
What do you mean?

946
59:47.772 --> 59:50.317
I can wait until you get back from the States.

947
59:52.110 --> 59:54.279
I'll be really good to you.

948
59:55.322 --> 59:56.406
[sighs softly]

949
59:58.909 --> 01:00:00.160
Third time's the charm,

950
01:00:01.328 --> 01:00:03.038
so I'm giving you one more chance.

951
01:00:03.955 --> 01:00:05.540
One last chance.

952
01:00:12.756 --> 01:00:14.758
Am I really that undesirable?

953
01:00:16.968 --> 01:00:18.386
[sighs]

954
01:00:20.764 --> 01:00:21.848
[stutters]

955
01:00:26.102 --> 01:00:29.606
People long ago believed that a solar eclipse

956
01:00:30.649 --> 01:00:34.069
was the heavenly dog in the sky swallowing the sun.

957
01:00:35.946 --> 01:00:38.114
Then the sun would be too hot for it,

958
01:00:38.198 --> 01:00:40.408
so it would spit it back out.

959
01:00:45.288 --> 01:00:46.831
That's what you're like to me.

960
01:00:48.416 --> 01:00:49.542
You're like the sun.

961
01:00:51.294 --> 01:00:52.295
Too hot.

962
01:00:58.843 --> 01:00:59.844
Then...

963
01:01:02.681 --> 01:01:03.932
Try swallowing it anyway.

964
01:01:05.475 --> 01:01:08.478
If it's too hot, you can spit it back out.

965
01:01:10.188 --> 01:01:12.941
Imagine how painful it must be to swallow the sun,

966
01:01:13.733 --> 01:01:15.485
only to have to spit it back out.

967
01:01:17.070 --> 01:01:19.364
I can't do that.

968
01:01:19.864 --> 01:01:21.408
I don't think I can.

969
01:01:25.787 --> 01:01:27.122
I don't want that anymore.

970
01:01:27.205 --> 01:01:29.833
I just want something easy and comfortable.

971
01:01:32.544 --> 01:01:35.296
That's the kind of guy I am.

972
01:01:40.051 --> 01:01:41.136
You're an idiot.

973
01:01:41.720 --> 01:01:42.846
You're such a coward.

974
01:01:44.806 --> 01:01:46.641
Stay that way for the rest of your life.

975
01:01:58.194 --> 01:01:59.988
[door lock beeps]

976
01:02:02.615 --> 01:02:04.617
[♪ emotional song playing]

977
01:02:21.634 --> 01:02:24.054
[rain pattering]

978
01:02:26.431 --> 01:02:27.599
What an idiot.

979
01:02:28.475 --> 01:02:30.351
Stay that way for the rest of your life. [sobbing]

980
01:02:59.672 --> 01:03:00.840
Let's get inside.

981
01:03:01.466 --> 01:03:02.675
You'll catch a cold.

982
01:03:34.082 --> 01:03:35.500
[Lim Youjin sobbing]

983
01:03:38.503 --> 01:03:39.504
Let go.

984
01:03:40.088 --> 01:03:41.422
Let go!

985
01:03:41.631 --> 01:03:42.715
[grunts]

986
01:03:43.133 --> 01:03:45.385
[crying]

987
01:04:05.780 --> 01:04:06.781
Once...

988
01:04:08.032 --> 01:04:10.118
I swallow something, I never spit it out.

989
01:04:13.538 --> 01:04:16.207
I'd never spit it out, even if it burned me alive.

990
01:04:20.712 --> 01:04:22.088
There's no going back.

991
01:04:24.090 --> 01:04:25.758
I have to see it through to the end.

992
01:04:30.388 --> 01:04:31.556
Do you still want this?

993
01:04:39.105 --> 01:04:43.776
[rain intensifies]

994
01:05:07.759 --> 01:05:11.679
BETWEEN STEPS

995
01:05:47.799 --> 01:05:49.509
[Park Minjae] How about we don't tell anyone

996
01:05:49.592 --> 01:05:51.177
that we're dating for now?

997
01:05:51.261 --> 01:05:52.512
He's asleep.

998
01:05:52.595 --> 01:05:54.764
[Lim Youjin] Kim Sejin. He's such a schemer. Okay?

999
01:05:54.847 --> 01:05:56.307
He's a crazy little suck-up.

1000
01:05:56.391 --> 01:05:58.476
But why do I even have to compete with him?

1001
01:05:58.559 --> 01:06:00.186
Park Minjae is mine.

1002
01:06:00.270 --> 01:06:01.354
We used to date.

1003
01:06:01.437 --> 01:06:02.522
You two used to date?

1004
01:06:02.605 --> 01:06:03.690
[Cha Seohyun] I'm sleeping over.

1005
01:06:03.773 --> 01:06:05.984
Me too. I can stay the night here too.

1006
01:06:06.067 --> 01:06:07.735
Like I said, she's my best friend.

1007
01:06:07.819 --> 01:06:11.030
You can't meet up with her alone or have her over at your place.

1008
01:06:11.114 --> 01:06:12.907
[Lim Youjin] Park Minjae is mine.

1009
01:06:12.991 --> 01:06:14.617
No one's taking you away from me.
